1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,362
This tutorial introduces four tools you
will use throughout RentAxis:

2
00:00:04,362 --> 00:00:08,288
the dashboard, global search,
notifications, and the Help Center.

3
00:00:08,288 --> 00:00:10,033
Begin on the dashboard.

4
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:13,523
The cards at the top summarize the active

5
00:00:13,523 --> 00:00:17,013
organization and the work visible to your
role.

6
00:00:17,013 --> 00:00:20,066
Read each label before interpreting a
number.

7
00:00:20,066 --> 00:00:23,556
A collection total, occupancy figure,
renewal follow-up, or

8
00:00:23,556 --> 00:00:27,046
open ticket count represents a different
operational question.

9
00:00:27,046 --> 00:00:29,663
Filters and the active organization
determine

10
00:00:29,663 --> 00:00:32,281
which records contribute to the result.

11
00:00:32,281 --> 00:00:36,207
Use dashboard figures as signals, then
open the related

12
00:00:36,207 --> 00:00:40,133
list or report when you need the
underlying records.

13
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:43,186
Next, open global search from the header.

14
00:00:43,186 --> 00:00:46,240
You can also use Control K on

15
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:48,857
Windows or Command K on macOS.

16
00:00:48,857 --> 00:00:53,655
Enter part of a known lease, renter,
cheque, or payment identifier.

17
00:00:53,655 --> 00:00:57,581
Search results are role-aware and
tenant-scoped, so you will

18
00:00:57,581 --> 00:01:01,071
only receive destinations you are allowed
to open.

19
00:01:01,071 --> 00:01:04,125
A super administrator can also find
organizations.

20
00:01:04,125 --> 00:01:08,487
Choose the prepared demo lease and confirm
that RentAxis opens

21
00:01:08,487 --> 00:01:12,849
the correct lease detail instead of a
general search-results page.

22
00:01:12,849 --> 00:01:15,903
Return to the dashboard and open
Notifications.

23
00:01:15,903 --> 00:01:20,701
The unread indicator shows items that have
not yet been acknowledged.

24
00:01:20,701 --> 00:01:25,064
Select one notification, review its title,
time, and message, then

25
00:01:25,064 --> 00:01:28,990
follow the related record when a link is
available.

26
00:01:28,990 --> 00:01:33,788
Return to the notification list and mark
the item as read.

27
00:01:33,788 --> 00:01:36,842
It should leave the Unread view
immediately

28
00:01:36,842 --> 00:01:39,895
while remaining available in the full
history.

29
00:01:39,895 --> 00:01:44,694
Use Mark All Read only after reviewing the
outstanding items; it

30
00:01:44,694 --> 00:01:49,056
is not a substitute for completing the
work they describe.

31
00:01:49,056 --> 00:01:51,237
Now open the Help Center.

32
00:01:51,237 --> 00:01:54,727
Help content is organized around roles and
capabilities.

33
00:01:54,727 --> 00:01:58,217
Search for Security Guard, open the
matching article,

34
00:01:58,217 --> 00:02:01,706
and compare its responsibilities with the
available navigation.

35
00:02:01,706 --> 00:02:06,069
Guided tours can point to controls inside
the running application,

36
00:02:06,069 --> 00:02:09,995
while articles explain the wider workflow
and safety rules.

37
00:02:09,995 --> 00:02:13,484
If search returns nothing, check spelling
and confirm

38
00:02:13,484 --> 00:02:16,974
that the feature is enabled for the
organization.

39
00:02:16,974 --> 00:02:20,464
To finish, return to the dashboard and
open

40
00:02:20,464 --> 00:02:23,954
global search once more with the keyboard
shortcut.

41
00:02:23,954 --> 00:02:28,316
Remember the pattern: use dashboard totals
to identify work, search

42
00:02:28,316 --> 00:02:32,242
to reach a record quickly, notifications
to respond to

43
00:02:32,242 --> 00:02:36,168
events, and Help whenever you need the
approved process.
